<title>SINGAPORE: LSI Logic says Asian revenue to hit 35 pct.</title>
<headline>LSI Logic says Asian revenue to hit 35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialised computer chip firm LSI Logic expects Asia to account for 35 percent of worldwide revenue within five years, up from a current 25 percent, W. Richard Marz, executive vice president geographic markets, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He told reporters at a briefing he expects the company's total worldwide revenue to reach around $2 to $3 billion within five years.</p>
<p>He said revenues were $1.27 billion in 1995 against net earnings of $238 million.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
